Findings
Critical: none identified in this scoped offline review.

HIGH — full configuration validation gates owned-engine stop
live-transport-qa.py:357-375, 450-460.
Cleanup calls inspect(cleanup=True), which requires not only captured CID/image/name/nonce ownership but also exact resource, network and mount configuration. If a still-owned engine's inspected PidsLimit changes after dispatch, inspect raises before the stop call. The fake-only probe changes only PidsLimit to0 after CLI join, preserving CID, image and nonce; the engine remains running, no stop is attempted, cleanup is unknown. This violates the requested stop-own-CID failure behavior. Unknown correctly prevents overall success, but does not compensate for the avoidable failure to attempt shutdown.
Required remediation: separate minimal exact ownership validation from operational configuration validation. Preserve any drift as failure/unknown, refuse further dispatch, but attempt bounded stop of the positively identified owned CID despite quota/cgroup/configuration proof failure. Never stop foreign/mismatched ownership. Add after-start drift regressions, preserving join-before-stop behavior and nonempty/missing cgroup unknown results. New source/tests require a new binding and independent review; do not waive this finding with the 31-test pass.

HIGH — preparation effects continue after approval/source invalidation during pull
live-transport-qa.py:397-419.
Authorization and input checks precede potentially long pull. After it returns, image inspection, volume creation and container creation occur before the next unchanged/authorize calls. If authorization has expired during pull, the harness still creates volume/container before the next authorize refuses. If source drifts during pull, the harness likewise creates volume/container before unchanged refuses. Fake-only probes reproduce both sequences. Neither starts nor dispatches, and the stopped created container is retained, but mutation already occurred outside the immediately revalidated scope.
Required remediation: immediately revalidate authorization and frozen inputs after long preparation and before each new externally mutating preparation/start/dispatch boundary (including volume create and container create), with cancellation/deadline checks. Cleanup remains permitted without fresh work authorization. Add regressions proving expiry/drift after pull causes no volume/container creation. Fresh parent receipts must bind the corrected implementation; do not treat time-valid initial authorization as permanently valid.

Medium/low: no additional blocking finding asserted. Normal single-operator trust is not hostile-same-UID protection; receipt identity authentication remains explicitly parent-owned.

